 ===== Current Limitations of the JUnit Gradle Plugin
 
-* Even though the build will fail if a test fails, the results will not be included in
-  the test report generated by Gradle.
-* With `runJunit4` set to `true`, the JUnit Gradle plugin takes over the responsibility
-  of running JUnit 4 tests, and the standard Gradle `test` task will no longer execute
-  JUnit 3 or JUnit 4 tests. Consequently, the results for JUnit 4 tests will not be
-  included in the standard test report generated by Gradle.
-
+* The results of any tests run via the JUnit Gradle plugin will not be included in the
+  standard test report generated by Gradle; however, the test results can be aggregated.
+  See the `reportsDir` property of the plugin.
 
